    "turn_text": "how that process works. For Nebraskans here, I have worked hard. I've been honest in my dealings with people. I believe I have the respect of my colleagues, and I work well with my colleagues, and we're able to get major legislation passed. For example, in 2007, we passed the largest tax relief package in the history of Nebraska. That was working with urban and rural senators and Democrats and Republicans. And so I believe I have that skill that I can take to Washington. Also, I'm the only rural candidate. I'm the only candidate in agriculture. I have a business, a small business. My husband and I have a family ranch and our three sons are back in the ranch with us. So I'm the candidate who has that business background, two of my opponents. have served the state, and they have served the state for many, many years. But I believe that people are looking for a different type of person to send to Washington because the times demanded. Our nation's in a crisis, and we have a lot at stake. And I think we need to change the type of person we send in to Washington.",
